  "H1": "Every closed-form evaluation point after32 zero-rate updates matches32 actual source Schedule-Free steps with real gradients and saved sampler state to max coordinate error <=1e-10. The base is bitwise unchanged; changing second moments are retained.",
  "H2": "All45 positive-history, nonstationary states move their evaluation weights despite learning rate zero. Report every state and any exception.",
  "H3": "For all six width64 P97/P193 checkpoints at750, the first zero-rate update lowers heldout CE but the50000-update endpoint has higher CE than initially and heldout accuracy below50%. Count every conjunct separately and retain failures.",
  "H4": "Negating every parameter of the actual model leaves all heldout logits unchanged within1e-6 at all45 checkpoints. The exact midpoint has uniform logits and zero strict-correct-winner fraction, even where both antipodal endpoints exceed99%.",
  "arithmetic": "CUDA float32 torch.compile(mode=max-autotune,fullgraph=True,dynamic=False) for all path evaluations. Independently checked CPU float64 source updates retain float32 RMS epsilon2^-23. The path formula is evaluated in float64 before copying into the compiled model.",
  "scope": "Counterfactual analysis of existing pinned runs, not new fits or a claim that zero-rate controls follow the original positive-rate future. The50000 endpoint is computed from the proved closed form, not simulated gradient updates. Positive stored total/maximum and default averaging powers are required. Negation is a symmetry/counterexample control, not an assertion that observed training visits antipodal states. No random-start convergence guarantee."
